   "key": "§ Training Load — end-to-end calculation > Layer 3 — Interpretation (Load & Trajectory surface)",
   "hash": "62b094c5706adfe9",
   "does": "Claims FormDescriptor thresholds >+10 Fresh, −5…+10 Held, −15…−5 Working, −25…−15 Tired, <−25 Very tired; ctlSlopePerWeek OLS over trailing 14 days ×7, 0 under 8 days; RampBand <−1.5 Easing down, −1.5…1.5 Holding steady, 1.5…3 Conservative, 3…8 Standard, >8 Rapid increase; compute order comeback → overreach → peaking → buildingBaseline unless >7 samples and week-ago CTL → delta = rampRate (fallback CTL difference when rampRate == 0) → TSB < −15 highStrain → delta > 1.5 building/rapidIncrease(>8) → delta < −1.5 detraining unless TSB < −5 maintaining → maintaining; peaking heuristic ATL < CTL by >10% over last 4 days; Foster monotony mean/SD over last 7 calendar days capped at 10, strain = week load × monotony, warning when monotony > 2.0 and strain > 1600. All verified in TrajectoryVerdict.swift:144-228 and FormDescriptor/RampBand inits, LoadTrajectoryLoader.swift:274-279, RecoveryScoreCalculator+Training.swift:24-45, FosterMonotonyWarning.swift:17-29, Constants+RecoveryScore.swift:230,237,244. TrainingDetailView uses the same isRaised rule (TrainingDetailView.swift:153-155).",
